        <div class="spec-number">★</div>
        <div class="spec-header-content">
          <div class="spec-name">BIDS Derivatives</div>
          <div class="spec-fullname">Processed / Derived Data Standard</div>
          <div class="spec-tags"><span class="tag tag-modal">preprocessed · maps · labels · atlases</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-card-body">
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">Source / Spec URL</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content"><a class="spec-link" href="https://bids-specification.readthedocs.io/en/stable/derivatives/introduction.html" target="_blank">bids-specification.readthedocs.io → derivatives</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">What it does</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content">Defines how to store outputs of BIDS-App pipelines in a standardized way — preprocessed images, statistical maps, parcellations, connectivity matrices, and quality control reports. Uses <code>derivatives/</code> folder with pipeline provenance encoded in dataset_description.json. Allows chaining of analysis pipelines while maintaining full reproducibility.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spec-card" data-domain="meta">
      <div class="spec-card-header">
        <div class="spec-number">★</div>
        <div class="spec-header-content">
          <div class="spec-name">BIDS Stats Model</div>
          <div class="spec-fullname">Statistical Modeling Specification</div>
          <div class="spec-tags"><span class="tag tag-modal">GLM · contrasts · group analysis</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-card-body">
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">Source / Spec URL</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content"><a class="spec-link" href="https://bids.neuroimaging.io/standards/bids_stats_model/index.html" target="_blank">bids.neuroimaging.io → bids_stats_model</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">What it does</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content">Defines a JSON-based specification for statistical models applied to BIDS neuroimaging data. Describes design matrices, HRF convolutions, contrast definitions, and group-level specifications in a software-agnostic way. Used by FitLins to produce FSL/SPM/nistats-compatible GLM analyses from a single model JSON file — enabling replication across software packages.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spec-card" data-domain="meta">
      <div class="spec-card-header">
        <div class="spec-number">★</div>
        <div class="spec-header-content">
          <div class="spec-name">BIDS Validator</div>
          <div class="spec-fullname">Dataset Integrity Validation Tool</div>
          <div class="spec-tags"><span class="tag tag-modal">all modalities</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-card-body">
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">Source / Spec URL</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content"><a class="spec-link" href="https://bids-standard.github.io/bids-validator/" target="_blank">bids-standard.github.io/bids-validator ↗ (web app)</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-section">
          <div class="spec-section-label">What it does</div>
          <div class="spec-section-content">Checks any BIDS dataset for compliance with the specification. Validates folder structure, file naming, required JSON fields, TSV column headers, and cross-file consistency. Available as a web app (drag &amp; drop), npm package, Python package, or Docker image. Required by OpenNeuro for all uploads.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

